%S A007789 1,1,0,4,1,0,13,4,27,1,1,0,25,13,0,16,1,27,37,4,0,1,1,0,25,25,81,52,1,
%T A007789 0,61,16,0,1,13,108,73,37,0,4,1,0,85,4,27,1,1,0,133,25,0,100,1,81,1,
%U A007789 52,0,1,1,0,121,61,351,64,25,0,133,4,0,13,1,108,145
%N A007789 a(n) = (1/n) * Sum_{x in (Z/nZ)^d} e^(2*Pi*i*det(circ(x))/n), the normalized Gauss sum of the d X d circulant determinant, where d=3.
%C A007789 From _Zoltan Reti_, Aug 16 2026: (Start)
%C A007789 For a vector x = (x_0,x_1,x_2) let circ(x) be the 3 X 3 circulant matrix with (i,j) entry x_{(j-i) mod 3}, so that det(circ(x)) = x_0^3 + x_1^3 + x_2^3 - 3*x_0*x_1*x_2.
%C A007789 Put the determinant in the exponent of an additive character and average over all residue vectors: a(n) is that average, normalized by n. It is a multiple Gauss sum in the sense of Berndt-Evans-Williams, with the 3-variable cubic det(circ) in place of the classical 1-variable square.
%C A007789 That a(n) is an integer at all is a theorem: det(circ(x)) is the algebra norm of Z[u]/(u^3-1), the norm is surjective on units, so the determinant histogram is constant on the classes gcd(c,n) = delta, and a Ramanujan-sum evaluation leaves a rational integer.
%C A007789 a(n) is multiplicative and is determined by the factorization of u^3 - 1 modulo the primes dividing n: at a prime p <> 3 the value is 2*p-1 if p == 1 (mod 3) (u^3-1 splits completely) and 1 if p == 2 (mod 3) (u^3-1 has an irreducible quadratic factor). The sequence therefore reads the splitting of p in the field Q(zeta_3).
%C A007789 a(n) = 0 if and only if 3 exactly divides n. (End)
%D A007789 B. C. Berndt, R. J. Evans and K. S. Williams, Gauss and Jacobi Sums, Wiley, 1998, p. 549.
%H A007789 Zoltan Reti, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21969894">The Multiple Gauss Sums Behind A007789-A007792</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A007789 Zoltan Reti, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21970261">Multiple Gauss Sums Generated by Circulant Matrices (Volume I of the two-volume work)</a>, Zenodo, 2026. Theorems 4.2, 5.10, 5.12, 5.15, 6.3, 6.14 and Appendix A.
%F A007789 From _Zoltan Reti_, Aug 16 2026: (Start)
%F A007789 a(m1*m2) = a(m1)*a(m2) for gcd(m1,m2) = 1.
%F A007789 a(p^k) = p^(k-1)*((k+1)*p - k) if p == 1 (mod 3).
%F A007789 a(p^k) = p^(2*floor(k/2)) if p == 2 (mod 3).
%F A007789 a(3) = 0, and a(3^k) = 3^(k+1) for k >= 2.
%F A007789 In particular, a(p) = 2*p-1 for p == 1 (mod 3) and a(p) = 1 for p == 2 (mod 3).
%F A007789 General master formula, valid for all d and all p not dividing d: if f_1, ..., f_r are the degrees of the irreducible factors of u^d - 1 over GF(p), then a_d(p) = p^(d-1) - (1/(p-1))*Product_{i=1..r} (p^(f_i) - 1). (End)
%e A007789 a(7) = 13: here n = 7 == 1 (mod 3), so u^3-1 splits completely over GF(7) and a(7) = 7^2 - 6^3/6 = 49 - 36 = 13.
%e A007789 a(9) = 27: n = 9 = 3^2 is the ramified square, a(9) = 3^3 = 27.
%e A007789 a(14) = 13: n = 14 = 2*7 and a(14) = a(2)*a(7) = 1*13 = 13, by multiplicativity.
%t A007789 dv[dd_, p_] := Sort[Flatten[Table[With[{f = MultiplicativeOrder[p, e]}, Table[f, {EulerPhi[e]/f}]], {e, Divisors[dd]}]]];
%t A007789 gt[p_, k_] := Module[{dg = dv[3, p], u, pp}, u = Times @@ (p^# - 1 & /@ dg); pp = PadRight[CoefficientList[Normal[Series[1/Times @@ (1 - x^# & /@ dg), {x, 0, k}]], x], k + 1]; p^(2*k) - u*Sum[pp[[s + 1]]*p^(2*k - 3 - s), {s, 0, k - 2}] - (u/(p - 1))*pp[[k]]*p^(k - 1)];
%t A007789 g[p_, k_] := If[p == 3, If[k == 1, 0, 3^(k + 1)], gt[p, k]];
%t A007789 a[n_] := If[n == 1, 1, Times @@ (g @@@ FactorInteger[n])];
%t A007789 Table[a[n], {n, 1, 73}] (* _Zoltan Reti_, Aug 29 2026 *)
%o A007789 (PARI) a(n) = {my(h=vector(n)); forvec(x=vector(3,i,[0,n-1]), h[(matdet(matrix(3,3,i,j,x[((j-i)%3)+1]))%n)+1]++); sumdiv(n, e, moebius(n/e)*h[(e%n)+1])/n} \\ direct from the definition, feasible for small n; _Zoltan Reti_, Aug 29 2026
